  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice.\r\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development shall not be occupied until details of the 5 long-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rThese details should demonstrate: \rLocation: Near entrances or main access, \rDesign: Stands \rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit, \rFull enclosed: 4 walls and a roof, \rAccessibility: 1.2m wide, Step-free, no obstructions. \r\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to conform to Enfield DMD policy 45 and promote sustainable modes of transport. \r",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance ENV 08/162, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details before the development is occupied or use commences and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation of the residential units hereby approved, the proposed new windows and doors shown on the approved plans shall be installed and be available for use.\r\rReason: In the interests of ensuring and protecting the amenities of future occupiers of the development.\r"
  ],
